IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VI, s 126 "Certificates": certificates and judgments (ss 126(1) to (3)),
-- garnishment (ss 126(4) to (9)), inspections (ss 126(10) to (13)), requirements to provide documents and information (ss 126(14)
-- to (20)), compliance (s 126(21)) and definitions (s 126(22)). Piece ei4. Layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- Conventions as in ei4-part-vi-review.l4. A power is a BOOLEAN whose FALSE means "this section does not give it"; a duty is a BOOLEAN
-- that is TRUE when the duty applies. The satisfaction of a judge ("if ... a judge is satisfied by information on oath that ...")
-- is carried as one BOOLEAN input for each limb the text lists, never worked out. Subsection (22) defines "authorized person" and
-- "judge"; the rules below take the outcome of those two definitions as BOOLEAN inputs and the two (22) rules compute them.
-- Hohfeld, for s 126: the Commission's power to certify, garnish, inspect and require is the liability of the person it is exercised
-- on; the occupant's immunity from entry into a dwelling-house without consent or warrant (s 126(11)) is the authorized person's disability.
-- A typographical oddity in the text: s 126(5) reads "Part VII.I" (capital letter I); it is read as Part VII.1 (see NOTES, finding 3).

§ `s 126 Certificates`

§§ `s 126(1) to (3) Certificates, judgments and costs`

-- The day after which 30 days since the default have expired. "On the expiration of 30 days after the default" is read as: the
-- 30 days end with day 30, so the amount may be certified from day 31 (fork F-ei4-6).
-- src:1904 | (b) in any other case, on the expiration of 30 days after the default.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(1)(b) (src:1904)
GIVEN `the day of the default` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 126(1)(b) the first day on which an unpaid amount may be certified when the person is not attempting to avoid payment` IS
    (`the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day of the default`) PLUS 1

-- src:1902 | 126 (1) An amount or part of an amount payable under Part I, II or VII.1 that has not been paid may be certified by the Commission
-- src:1903 | (a) without delay, if in the opinion of the Commission the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment; and
-- src:1904 | (b) in any other case, on the expiration of 30 days after the default.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(1) (src:1902-1904)
GIVEN `the Part under which the amount is payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
      `the amount has not been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Commission the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the default` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission would certify the amount` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` IF
        (   `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part I`
         OR `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part II`
         OR `the Part under which the amount is payable` EQUALS `Part VII.1`)
    AND `the amount has not been paid`
    AND (   `in the opinion of the Commission the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment`
         OR `the day on which the Commission would certify the amount` AT LEAST
                `s 126(1)(b) the first day on which an unpaid amount may be certified when the person is not attempting to avoid payment` `the day of the default`)

-- The registered certificate has the force of a Federal Court judgment for the amount plus interest to the day of payment.
-- The interest "as provided for in this Act" is s 80.1 and the regulations under it (out of range: piece ei3), so it is an input.
-- NOTHING when the certificate has not been produced to the Federal Court and registered: the subsection then says nothing.
-- src:1906 | (2) On production to the Federal Court, the resulting certificate shall be registered in the Court and when registered has the same force and effect, and all proceedings may be taken, as if the certificate were a judgment obtained in the Court for a debt of the amount specified in the certificate plus interest to the day of payment as provided for in this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(2) (src:1906)
GIVEN `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount specified in the certificate` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest to the day of payment as provided for in this Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 80.1 and its regulations (piece ei3)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 126(2) the debt for which the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court` IS
    IF `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered`
    THEN JUST (`the amount specified in the certificate` PLUS `the interest to the day of payment as provided for in this Act`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1908 | (3) All reasonable costs and charges attendant on the registration of the certificate are recoverable in like manner as if they had been certified and the certificate had been registered under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(3) (src:1908)
GIVEN `the costs and charges are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs and charges are attendant on the registration of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(3) the costs and charges are recoverable as if they had been certified and the certificate registered` IF
        `the costs and charges are reasonable`
    AND `the costs and charges are attendant on the registration of the certificate`

§§ `s 126(4) to (9) Garnishment`

-- The Commission's power over a third party who owes the debtor money; the debtor is the person liable to pay under Part I, II or VII.1
-- or under subsection (7). The Commission's knowledge or suspicion is its own state of mind, so it is an input.
-- src:1910 | (4) If the Commission has knowledge or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment under Part I, II or VII.1 or under subsection (7), it may, by a notice served personally or sent by a confirmed delivery service, require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person in whole or in part to the Receiver General on account of the second person’s liability.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(4) (src:1910)
GIVEN `the Commission has knowledge or suspects that the first person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to the second person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second person is liable to make a payment under Part I, II or VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second person is liable to make a payment under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` IF
        `the Commission has knowledge or suspects that the first person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to the second person`
    AND (`the second person is liable to make a payment under Part I, II or VII.1` OR `the second person is liable to make a payment under subsection (7)`)
    AND (`the notice is served personally` OR `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service`)

-- Future payments of remuneration. Paragraph (a): the requirement covers every later payment until the liability is satisfied.
-- src:1912 | (5) If the Commission has, under subsection (4), required an employer to pay to the Receiver General on account of an insured person’s liability under Part I or II or an individual’s liability under Part VII.I, money otherwise payable by the employer to the insured person or the individual, as the case may be, as remuneration,
-- src:1913 | (a) the requirement is applicable to all future payments by the employer to the insured person or individual, as the case may be, as remuneration until the liability under that Part is satisfied; and
-- src:1914 | (b) the employer shall make payments to the Receiver General out of each payment of remuneration of the amount that may be stipulated by the Commission in the notice mentioned in subsection (4).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(5)(a) (src:1912-1914)
GIVEN `the Commission has under subsection (4) required an employer to pay to the Receiver General, on account of an insured person's liability under Part I or II or an individual's liability under Part VII.1, money otherwise payable by the employer as remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is a future payment by the employer to the insured person or individual as remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability under that Part has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment` IF
        `the Commission has under subsection (4) required an employer to pay to the Receiver General, on account of an insured person's liability under Part I or II or an individual's liability under Part VII.1, money otherwise payable by the employer as remuneration`
    AND `the payment is a future payment by the employer to the insured person or individual as remuneration`
    AND NOT (`the liability under that Part has been satisfied`)

-- Paragraph (b): out of each payment the employer pays the Receiver General the amount stipulated in the notice. NOTHING when the
-- requirement is not applicable to the payment.
-- src:1912 | (5) If the Commission has, under subsection (4), required an employer to pay to the Receiver General on account of an insured person’s liability under Part I or II or an individual’s liability under Part VII.I, money otherwise payable by the employer to the insured person or the individual, as the case may be, as remuneration,
-- src:1913 | (a) the requirement is applicable to all future payments by the employer to the insured person or individual, as the case may be, as remuneration until the liability under that Part is satisfied; and
-- src:1914 | (b) the employer shall make payments to the Receiver General out of each payment of remuneration of the amount that may be stipulated by the Commission in the notice mentioned in subsection (4).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(5)(b) (src:1912-1914)
GIVEN `the Commission has under subsection (4) required an employer to pay to the Receiver General, on account of an insured person's liability under Part I or II or an individual's liability under Part VII.1, money otherwise payable by the employer as remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is a future payment by the employer to the insured person or individual as remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability under that Part has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount stipulated by the Commission in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 126(5)(b) the amount the employer must pay to the Receiver General out of the payment of remuneration` IS
    IF `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment`
            `the Commission has under subsection (4) required an employer to pay to the Receiver General, on account of an insured person's liability under Part I or II or an individual's liability under Part VII.1, money otherwise payable by the employer as remuneration`
            `the payment is a future payment by the employer to the insured person or individual as remuneration`
            `the liability under that Part has been satisfied`
    THEN JUST `the amount stipulated by the Commission in the notice`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Discharge: the receipt is a good and sufficient discharge of "the original liability" to the extent of the payment. "The original
-- liability" is read as the liability of the person who paid, to the person the money was otherwise payable to (fork F-ei4-9).
-- src:1916 | (6) The receipt of the Commission for money paid as required under subsection (4) or (5) is a good and sufficient discharge of the original liability to the extent of the payment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(6) (src:1916)
GIVEN `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of money paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 126(6) the amount of the original liability that the receipt discharges` IS
    IF `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required under subsection (4) or (5)`
    THEN JUST `the amount of money paid`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1916 | (6) The receipt of the Commission for money paid as required under subsection (4) or (5) is a good and sufficient discharge of the original liability to the extent of the payment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(6) (src:1916)
GIVEN `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of money paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the original liability` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 126(6) the original liability that remains after the discharge` IS
    CONSIDER `s 126(6) the amount of the original liability that the receipt discharges` `the Commission has given a receipt for money paid as required under subsection (4) or (5)` `the amount of money paid`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST discharged THEN
        IF `the original liability` AT LEAST discharged
        THEN JUST (`the original liability` MINUS discharged)
        ELSE JUST 0

-- src:1918 | (7) An amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection (4) or (5) is a debt due to Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(7) (src:1918)
GIVEN `the amount required to be paid by a notice under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid as required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 126(7) the amount not paid as required, which is a debt due to Her Majesty` IS
    IF `the amount required to be paid by a notice under subsection (4) or (5)` GREATER THAN `the amount paid as required`
    THEN `the amount required to be paid by a notice under subsection (4) or (5)` MINUS `the amount paid as required`
    ELSE 0

-- src:1920 | (8) A notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to the name or style under which a person carries on business if the person carries on business under a name or style other than their own name and, in the case of personal service, the notice is validly served if it is left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the addressee.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(8) (src:1920)
GIVEN `the person carries on business under a name or style other than their own name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(8) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to the name or style under which the person carries on business` IF
    `the person carries on business under a name or style other than their own name`

-- src:1920 | (8) A notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to the name or style under which a person carries on business if the person carries on business under a name or style other than their own name and, in the case of personal service, the notice is validly served if it is left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the addressee.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(8) (src:1920)
GIVEN `the person carries on business under a name or style other than their own name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is addressed to that name or style` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the addressee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(8) the notice is validly served` IF
        `the person carries on business under a name or style other than their own name`
    AND `the notice is addressed to that name or style`
    AND `the notice is served personally`
    AND `the notice is left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the addressee`

-- src:1922 | (9) A notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to a partnership name if the person who is to receive it carries on business in partnership under that name and, in the case of personal service, the notice is validly served if it is served on one of the partners or left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the partnership.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(9) (src:1922)
GIVEN `the person who is to receive the notice carries on business in partnership under that name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(9) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to a partnership name` IF
    `the person who is to receive the notice carries on business in partnership under that name`

-- src:1922 | (9) A notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to a partnership name if the person who is to receive it carries on business in partnership under that name and, in the case of personal service, the notice is validly served if it is served on one of the partners or left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the partnership.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(9) (src:1922)
GIVEN `the person who is to receive the notice carries on business in partnership under that name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is addressed to the partnership name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served on one of the partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(9) the notice is validly served` IF
        `the person who is to receive the notice carries on business in partnership under that name`
    AND `the notice is addressed to the partnership name`
    AND `the notice is served personally`
    AND (   `the notice is served on one of the partners`
         OR `the notice is left with an adult person employed at the place of business of the partnership`)

§§ `s 126(10) to (13) Inspections`

-- The authority to inspect or examine a document.
-- src:1924 | (10) An authorized person may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, inspect or examine any document that relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any benefits payable under this Act and, for those purposes, the authorized person may
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(10) (src:1924)
GIVEN `is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates or may relate to the amount of any benefits payable under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` IF
        `is an authorized person`
    AND `the inspection is at a reasonable time`
    AND `the inspection is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV`
    AND (   `the document relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account`
         OR `the document relates or may relate to the amount of any benefits payable under this Act`)

-- The occupant's immunity (and the authorized person's disability): a dwelling-house may be entered only with the occupant's
-- consent or under a warrant issued under subsection (12). TRUE means the entry is permitted so far as subsection (11) is concerned.
-- For a premises or place that is not a dwelling-house the subsection says nothing, so it does not stand in the way.
-- src:1928 | (11) If the premises or place is a dwelling-house, an authorized person may only enter with the consent of the occupant or under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (12).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(11) (src:1928)
GIVEN `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents to the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(11) subsection (11) permits the authorized person to enter the premises or place` IF
        NOT (`the premises or place is a dwelling-house`)
    OR `the occupant consents to the entry`
    OR `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (12)`

-- Paragraph (a), "subject to subsection (11)": entry where the authorized person believes on reasonable grounds that persons are or
-- were employed there or that records or books of account are or should be kept there.
-- src:1924 | (10) An authorized person may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, inspect or examine any document that relates or may relate to the information that is or should be contained in the records or books of account or to the amount of any benefits payable under this Act and, for those purposes, the authorized person may
-- src:1925 | (a) subject to subsection (11), enter any premises or place where the authorized person believes, on reasonable grounds, that persons are or were employed or where any records or books of account are or should be kept; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(10)(a) (src:1924-1925)
GIVEN `is an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorized person believes, on reasonable grounds, that persons are or were employed at the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorized person believes, on reasonable grounds, that records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents to the entry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` IF
        `is an authorized person`
    AND `the entry is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV`
    AND (   `the authorized person believes, on reasonable grounds, that persons are or were employed at the premises or place`
         OR `the authorized person believes, on reasonable grounds, that records or books of account are or should be kept at the premises or place`)
    AND `s 126(11) subsection (11) permits the authorized person to enter the premises or place`
            `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents to the entry` `the entry is under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (12)`

-- Paragraph (b): the owner, occupant or person in charge must give reasonable assistance, answer proper questions and, if required, attend.
-- src:1926 | (b) require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to give the authorized person all reasonable assistance and to answer all proper questions relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, and, for that purpose, require the owner, occupant or person in charge to attend at the premises or place with the authorized person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(10)(b) (src:1926)
GIVEN `is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an authorized person is exercising the power in subsection (10) at the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance asked for is reasonable, or the question asked is proper and relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(10)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give the assistance or answer the question` IF
        `is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place`
    AND `an authorized person is exercising the power in subsection (10) at the premises or place`
    AND `the assistance asked for is reasonable, or the question asked is proper and relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV`

-- src:1930 | (12) If, on ex parte application by the Commission, a judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:1931 | (a) there are reasonable grounds for believing that a dwelling-house is a premises or place mentioned in subsection (10),
-- src:1932 | (b) entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, and
-- src:1933 | (c) entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused,
-- src:1934 | the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(12) (src:1930-1934)
GIVEN `the Commission has applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that a dwelling-house is a premises or place mentioned in subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` IF
        `the Commission has applied ex parte`
    AND `is a judge`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds for believing that a dwelling-house is a premises or place mentioned in subsection (10)`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused`

-- The closing words "to the extent that access has been or may be expected to be refused and that the document is or may be expected
-- to be kept in the dwelling-house" qualify both paragraphs, so they are conditions of the one rule.
-- src:1936 | (13) If the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, the judge may
-- src:1937 | (a) order the occupant of the dwelling-house to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to any document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house, and
-- src:1938 | (b) make such other order as is appropriate in the circumstances to carry out the purposes of this Act, other than Part IV,
-- src:1939 | to the extent that access has been or may be expected to be refused and that the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(13) (src:1936-1939)
GIVEN `the judge is hearing an application under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access has been or may be expected to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` IF
        `the judge is hearing an application under subsection (12)`
    AND `the judge is not satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV`
    AND `access has been or may be expected to be refused`
    AND `the document is or may be expected to be kept in the dwelling-house`

§§ `s 126(14) to (20) Requirement to provide documents and information`

-- Subsection (15) is a bar on the Commission, in favour of a third party (and of the unnamed persons): no requirement relating to
-- unnamed persons without a judge's authorization first obtained. TRUE means the bar applies to the requirement.
-- src:1945 | (15) The Commission shall not impose on any person, in this section referred to as a “third party”, a requirement under subsection (14) to provide information or any document relating to one or more unnamed persons unless it first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection (16).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(15) (src:1945)
GIVEN `the requirement is imposed on a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(15) the Commission shall not impose the requirement on the third party` IF
        `the requirement is imposed on a third party`
    AND `the requirement relates to one or more unnamed persons`
    AND NOT (`the Commission has first obtained the authorization of a judge under subsection (16)`)

-- src:1941 | (14) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, but subject to subsection (15), the Commission may for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require that any person provide, within such reasonable time as is stated in the notice,
-- src:1942 | (a) any information or additional information, including any information return or supplementary return; or
-- src:1943 | (b) any document.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(14) (src:1941-1943)
GIVEN `the requirement is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states a reasonable time within which the person must provide the information or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is for information or additional information, including an information return or supplementary return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is for a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (15) bars the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` IF
        `the requirement is for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV`
    AND (`the notice is served personally` OR `the notice is sent by a confirmed delivery service`)
    AND `the notice states a reasonable time within which the person must provide the information or document`
    AND (`the requirement is for information or additional information, including an information return or supplementary return` OR `the requirement is for a document`)
    AND NOT (`subsection (15) bars the requirement`)

-- Paragraphs (16)(c) and (d) are repealed (src:1950); they are not encoded.
-- src:1947 | (16) On ex parte application by the Commission, a judge may, subject to such conditions as the judge considers appropriate, authorize the Commission to impose on a third party a requirement under subsection (14) relating to an unnamed person or more than one unnamed person, in this section referred to as the “group”, if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:1948 | (a) the person or group is ascertainable; and
-- src:1949 | (b) the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act, other than Part IV.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(16) (src:1947-1949)
GIVEN `the Commission has applied ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act, other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(16) the judge may authorize the Commission to impose on a third party a requirement relating to an unnamed person or group` IF
        `the Commission has applied ex parte`
    AND `is a judge`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with any duty or obligation under this Act, other than Part IV`

-- src:1952 | (17) If the authorization is granted, it shall be served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (14).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(17) (src:1952)
GIVEN `the authorization is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(17) the authorization must be served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (14)` IF
    `the authorization is granted`

-- src:1954 | (18) If the authorization is granted, a third party on whom it is served may, within 15 days after it is served, apply for a review of the authorization to the judge who granted it or, if the judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(18) (src:1954)
GIVEN `the day on which the authorization is served on the third party` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 126(18) the last day on which the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` IS
    `the last day of` 15 `days after` `the day on which the authorization is served on the third party`

-- src:1954 | (18) If the authorization is granted, a third party on whom it is served may, within 15 days after it is served, apply for a review of the authorization to the judge who granted it or, if the judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(18) (src:1954)
GIVEN `the authorization is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party is the person on whom the authorization is served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the authorization is served on the third party` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application for review is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(18) the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` IF
        `the authorization is granted`
    AND `the third party is the person on whom the authorization is served`
    AND `the day on which the application for review is made` AT MOST
            `s 126(18) the last day on which the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` `the day on which the authorization is served on the third party`

-- src:1956 | (19) On hearing the application, the judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (16)(a) and (b) have been met and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(19) (src:1956)
DECLARE `ei4 What the judge may do on a review of an authorization` IS ONE OF
    `s 126(19) the judge may cancel the authorization`
    `s 126(19) the judge may confirm or vary the authorization`

-- src:1956 | (19) On hearing the application, the judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (16)(a) and (b) have been met and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(19) (src:1956)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (16)(a) and (b) have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `ei4 What the judge may do on a review of an authorization`
DECIDE `s 126(19) what the judge may do on hearing the application for review` IS
    IF `the judge is satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (16)(a) and (b) have been met`
    THEN `s 126(19) the judge may confirm or vary the authorization`
    ELSE `s 126(19) the judge may cancel the authorization`

-- src:1958 | (20) If a document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with subsection (10) or (14),
-- src:1959 | (a) the person by whom it is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided, or any other person acting for the Commission, may make one or more copies, or have them made; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(20)(a) (src:1958-1959)
GIVEN `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with subsection (10) or (14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the person by whom the document is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is another person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(20)(a) the person may make one or more copies, or have them made` IF
        `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with subsection (10) or (14)`
    AND (   `is the person by whom the document is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided`
         OR `is another person acting for the Commission`)

-- src:1958 | (20) If a document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with subsection (10) or (14),
-- src:1960 | (b) any document appearing to be certified by the Commission or an authorized person to be a copy made under this subsection is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(20)(b) (src:1958) (src:1960)
GIVEN `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with subsection (10) or (14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document appears to be certified by the Commission or an authorized person to be a copy made under subsection (20)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(20)(b) the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document with the same probative force as the original` IF
        `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with subsection (10) or (14)`
    AND `the document appears to be certified by the Commission or an authorized person to be a copy made under subsection (20)`

§§ `s 126(21) Compliance`

-- No person shall hinder, molest or interfere, or prevent or attempt to prevent; and every person shall, unless unable to do so, do
-- everything required by or under the section. A person contravenes the subsection by doing any of the first group, or by failing the
-- second without being unable.
-- src:1962 | (21) No person shall hinder, molest or interfere with any person doing anything that the person is authorized to do by or under this section or prevent or attempt to prevent any person from doing any such thing and, notwithstanding any other Act or law, every person shall, unless unable to do so, do everything required by or under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(21) (src:1962)
GIVEN `hinders, molests or interferes with a person doing anything that the person is authorized to do by or under section 126` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prevents or attempts to prevent a person from doing anything that the person is authorized to do by or under section 126` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fails to do everything required of the person by or under section 126` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is unable to do everything required of the person by or under section 126` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` IF
        `hinders, molests or interferes with a person doing anything that the person is authorized to do by or under section 126`
    OR `prevents or attempts to prevent a person from doing anything that the person is authorized to do by or under section 126`
    OR (    `fails to do everything required of the person by or under section 126`
        AND NOT (`is unable to do everything required of the person by or under section 126`))

§§ `s 126(22) Definitions`

-- src:1965 | authorized person means a person authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of this section; (personne autorisée)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(22) "authorized person" (src:1965)
GIVEN `is authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(22) authorized person` IF
    `is authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of section 126`

-- src:1966 | judge means a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises or a judge of the Federal Court. (juge)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 126(22) "judge" (src:1966)
GIVEN `is a judge of a superior court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a judge of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 126(22) judge` IF
        (`is a judge of a superior court` AND `the court has jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises`)
    OR `is a judge of the Federal Court`

